course: dictionary
lesson: 12801
title: Lifting words: elevate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Elevate is a verb, and it has three main meanings. It can mean to lift something up, to give someone a higher rank, or to make something better. The word elevates, elevated and elevating show it happening now, in the past, or while it is going on. «Ben elevated his sore foot on a pillow.» Ben lifted his foot up higher, so elevated means raised.
explain: Read the words around the word to find the right meaning. «The team elevated Sara to captain.» The clue is the word captain: a higher rank. «A cup of hot cocoa can elevate your mood on a cold day.» Here elevate means to improve, because a cocoa cannot lift your mood up the way a pillow lifts your foot.
explain: Elevation is a related word that shows up in geography. «The village sits at an elevation of 800 metres.» Elevation means height above sea level. Be careful: elevate and elevation are not the same word, but they come from the same idea of rising up.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you think elevated means raised, try «Ben raised his sore foot on a pillow.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. If it makes no sense, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Elevate means to lift something up to a higher position.
fact: Elevate can also mean to give someone a higher rank or more importance.
fact: Elevate can mean to make something better, such as your mood or a meal.
fact: In first aid, you elevate an injured leg or arm to reduce swelling or bleeding.
fact: Elevation means height above sea level, so a mountain has a high elevation.
exercise: «Ben elevated his sore foot on a pillow.» What does elevated mean here? | Washed in cold water | Pressed very hard | Hidden under the bed | *Raised up
exercise: Mrs Patel was elevated to head teacher last year. What does this mean? | She was told to leave the school | *She was given a higher job | She was moved to a smaller room | She was given a day off
exercise: In geography, what does elevation mean? | How many people live there | *Height above sea level | How far it is to the shops | How deep a lake is
test: «A cup of cocoa can elevate your mood.» What does elevate your mood mean? | *Make your mood better | Measure your mood | Make your mood colder | Hide your mood
test: Which word is closest in meaning to elevate, as in lift? | *raise | lower | forget | break
exam: «The nurse elevated the injured arm above the heart to reduce swelling.» What does elevated mean here? | *Raised higher | Cooled in a bag of ice | Wrapped tightly in a bandage | Pushed down flat
